      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشْتَغٍ</span></b>  One <i>who separates himself from every
yoke-fellow,</i> or <i>familiar:</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <i>one whose age</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِنُّهُ</span>) <i>is deficient:</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  in both of these senses expl.
as an epithet applied by Ru-beh to a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَاعِىّ</span> [or
boy four spans in height]. (TA.)

